# gptokeyb map for Vita3K-Plus on dArkOS.
#
# Weston/libinput ignores gamepads ("device is a joystick or a gamepad,
# ignoring"), so the Qt frontend never sees the handheld's buttons. gptokeyb
# turns them into uinput key events, which Weston forwards to Qt as a keyboard.
#
# Those keys also drive the emulated Vita pad: CtrlKeyboardFilter is installed
# as an event filter on the game window (main_window.cpp), so it runs before
# GameWindow::keyPressEvent's ignore(). And gptokeyb does not EVIOCGRAB the pad
# -- Vita3K's SDL has the same /dev/input/eventN open -- so every button arrives
# twice, once as a key and once as an SDL pad button. The keys below are chosen
# so both paths land on the *same* Vita button; psvita-launch.sh primes Vita3K's
# keyboard bindings to match (cross=Enter, circle=Escape, square=Space,
# triangle=Backspace, start=Insert, select=Delete, L1/R1/L2/R2=PageUp/PageDown/
# Home/End). Keeping a=enter also means A still activates items in the Qt GUI.
#
# Select+Start is gptokeyb's own exit combo and kills Vita3K.
back = delete
start = insert
a = enter
b = esc
x = space
y = backspace
l1 = pageup
r1 = pagedown
l2 = home
r2 = end
up = up
down = down
left = left
right = right
left_analog_up = up
left_analog_down = down
left_analog_left = left
left_analog_right = right